    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are support classes, not test cases). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based level-4 rule for membership level.\n\n**`OwnerDerivations.membershipLevel`** (`src/main/java/.../model/OwnerDerivations.java`) \u2014 the pure derivation now takes `registrationDate` and an `asOf` date. It computes the creation-time factors as before (base 1, +1 for an email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3), then adds one more level to reach 4 only when tenure \u2014 the whole days from `registrationDate` to `asOf` (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between`) \u2014 exceeds 365. Added the `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`Owner.getMembershipLevel`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`) \u2014 passes `this.registrationDate` and `LocalDate.now()`, so the level rises to 4 once an owner's tenure passes 365 days and is recomputed each call.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipLevel` schema description, and raised `maximum` from 3 to 4.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is \"today\", its tenure is 0, so it is capped at level 3 \u2014 exactly what the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test asserts (a new owner with an email and no namesake gets 1 + 1 + 1 = 3, not 4). Tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
